{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385360-fields-for-the-technocracy-reloaded","id":1385360,"title":"Fields for the Technocracy, Reloaded","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-02T23:17:18-07:00","id":1385360,"title":"Fields for the Technocracy, Reloaded","content":"This is a reboot of an earlier thread I set up, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/758179-fields-for-the-technocracy\">Fields for the Technocracy</a>. Sadly, I lost my focus on the original thread and it derailed. I am attempting here a more modest proposal.<br /> <br /> The idea is that the Technocracy doesn't use the same Spheres that the Traditions do. This is because the Order of Reason predates the Traditions. Mind you, there are many similarities; these come from the fact that the order of reason was originally founded by the Craftmasons and other factions that had descended from the same group of mages that eventually became the Order of Hermes. But the two systems are not identical.<br /> <br /> I'm basing this on the variant technocratic spheres that are described in M20, although what I'm presenting here involves more extensive changes then what the Sphere variants provide. I'm calling them Fields instead of Spheres in reference to their somewhat different organizational structure, but in practice they use the same rules as Spheres do. The only thing that really differs is which ones you need to perform a given Effect: for example, there are things that fall under the Field of Time but wouldn't be covered by the Sphere of Time that the Traditions use. I've tried to keep the names distinct to minimize confusion; but it wasn't always reasonable to do so. <br /> <br /> The nine Fields of Enlightened Science are: <br /> <br /> Energy (Force Dynamics)<br /> Matter (Material Science)<br /> Life (Biological Science)<br /> <br /> Space (Void Correspondence)<br /> Time (Temporal Mechanics)<br /> Void (Dimensional Science)<br /> <br /> Data (Information Science)<br /> Mind (Enlightened Psychology)<br /> Utility (Primal Utility)<br /> <br /> They often have more elaborate names, especially when a Scientist is discussing a specialty of a Field; but per the principle of Huffman Encoding, the names that get used most often tend to contract in length the more they're used; so while I'm including long-winded alternate names for each, I expect that the short names will tend to be used in practice. <br /> <br /> Here's how the Spheres map to the Fields:<br /> <br /> <i>Correspondence Effects</i> get split between Data and Space, with Data getting the Digital Web stuff and the stuff about Sympathetic Connections, while Space gets the measuring and control of spatial relationships. Each gets its own version of the Correspondence Range table, with Data's table being based on the one first introduced in the Revised NWO Convention Book while Space's table is based on the one that first appeared in the Revised Void Engineers Convention Book. <br /> <br /> <i>Entropy Effects</i> get split between Data and Time, with Data getting those dealing with order and chaos \u2014 \u201cfate\u201d and \u201cluck\u201d \u2014 while Time gets those that deal with decay, but rephrased In terms of aging. <br /> <br /> <i>Forces Effects</i> mostly go to Energy; but the ones having to do with motion and gravity go instead to Space. <br /> <br /> <i>Life Effects</i> go to Life. It's possible that some Effects move to different levels in the transition (Shapeshifting isn't something that Technocrats are into; but they're arguably more capable with inflicting and curing diseases); but other than some internal rearrangement, they essentially cover the same ground. <br /> <br /> <i>Matter Effects</i> likewise go to Material Science. Much like Biological Science is less about shapeshifting and more about manipulating health, Material Science is less about transmutation and more about manipulation of mechanisms. <br /> <br /> <i>Mind Effects</i> go directly to Enlightened Psychology as is, though the Technocracy has gone further than the Traditions both in terms of teaching techniques and in terms of altering the Consensus. There are also some Mind-like Effects added to Information Science, such as sensor spoofing (manipulation of perceptions) and memory alteration. <br /> <br /> <i>Prime Effects</i> get split between Void and Utility, with Void getting the concept of Primal Energy (e.g., blades made of Primal Energy) and most forms of Tass, while Utility gets everything that Primal Utility gets in M20 (such as Primal Ventures). Utility also holds the secrets of the Technocracy's ability to set up mass production lines for Devices and Principiae. <br /> <br /> <i>Spirit Effects</i> go to Dimensional Science (or \u201cVoid\u201d) as per M20. <br /> <br /> <i>Time Effects</i> go to Temporal Mechanics. <br /> <br /> Turning this around: <br /> <br /> <i>Energy</i> gets most of the Forces Effects, except for the ones involving gravity and motion. <br /> <br /> <i>Matter</i> gets all of the Matter Effects, but rearranges some of them to emphasize mechanics over alchemy. <br /> <br /> <i>Life</i> gets all of the Life Effects, but rearranges some of them to emphasize vitality over shapeshifting. <br /> <br /> <i>Space</i> gets geometric manipulation from Correspondence (including teleportation) plus gravity manipulation and conveyance Effects from Forces. <br /> <br /> <i>Time</i> gets all of the Time Effects, plus Entropy Effects pertaining to decay and death (rephrased as \u201cage control\u201d). <br /> <br /> <i>Void</i> gets everything from Spirit (but with summoning, binding and warding de-emphasized in favor of Gauntlet manipulation), plus aspects of Prime that deal with things made of Prime. In particular, where summoning something ex-nihilo would require two dots of the Prime Sphere, it requires two dots of Void (to extract the necessary \u201czero-point energy\u201d from the Quantum Vacuum). <br /> <br /> <i>Data</i> draws Digital Web access and Sympathetic Connections from Correspondence, and manipulation of order and chaos from Entropy; it also gets effects for dealing with the manipulation of sensors and digital records that echo Mind Effects, and effects for summoning, binding and warding digital entities that echo Spirit Effects. It also gets the \u201cspatial manipulation\u201d stuff from Correspondence, but <i>only</i> in the context of the Digital Web: that is, it can teleport, create gateways, co-locate, etc., just like Correspondence can, but <i>only</i> in the Digital Web. This is different from the Data Sphere variant described in M20, drastically limiting its Correspondence-related capabilities, and is the reason why I'm okay with it having so many other capabilities derived from Entropy, Mind, and Spirit. <br /> <br /> <i>Mind</i> gets all of the Mind Effects (except possibly language manipulation, which may be ported over to Data) and a few new Effects that are unique to the Technocracy. <br /> <br /> <i>Utility</i> gets the bulk of the Prime Effects, excepting only the ones that involve some sort of tangible manifestation of Primal Energy. It also skews the results toward Wonder crafting and tapping into sources of Quintessence that Prime doesn't even consider. <br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> That's the basics. <br /> <br /> I was tempted to transfer the \u201ctangible manifestations of Quintessence\u201d to Energy instead of Void to help offset the loss of Forces' gravity and motion Effects; but I stuck to Void because I think it's conceptually a better for there. <br /> <br /> The added functionality that Mind and Utility get are there to help explain the Union's current dominance: the former has given them an edge with the Consensus, and the latter explains the Requisitions Background. <br /> <br /> The intended changes to Matter and Life are to bring those two Fields in line with how the Technocracy tends to use them. <br /> <br /> Space and Data are set up the way they are to reflect the very different perspectives on Correspondence found in the NWO and VEs respectively. <br /> <br /> The Fields don't have an Entropy equivalent because Enlightened Science doesn't really work that way. Manipulation of order and chaos went to Data by thinking of them as identifying and manipulating small-p patterns, while the death and decay stuff went to Time mainly to bolster it; but thinking of it in terms of age manipulation works reasonably well. <br /> <br /> Most if not all of these Fields have parallels to branches of science: Energy, Space, and Time together represent physics; Matter covers chemistry and mechanics; Life covers most of the Life Sciences (though ecology might require some Data to deal with the intricate networks of interactions between different lifeforms). Data is all about the formal sciences: logic, mathematics, computer science, linguistics, etc. Mind is all about the bulk of the social sciences, save only for economics which is handled by Utility. <br /> <br /> Void is the only Field that doesn't correlate with a modern branch of science; instead, it deals with those phenomena that the Technocracy is attempting to excise from the Consensus: spirits, ghosts, alternate realities, mystical energies, etc. <br /> <br /> Thoughts? Suggestions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-29-2020, 11:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T23:33:38-07:00","id":1385363,"title":"","content":"I love the idea of breaking up Space and Data by letting Data eat Entropy (with the decay stuff being moved to Time). That makes perfect sense.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m a bit shakier on how the ex nihlo Prime energy stuff fits with Void. Also does this require Iteration X device inventors to delve into the Syndicate\u2019s Utility paradigm? Wouldn\u2019t they deal with Prime as generatable energy rather than abstract utility value?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T00:46:43-07:00","id":1385370,"title":"","content":"A couple of possibilities to consider: <br /> <br /> 1. I had originally been thinking of doing something like <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/428316-the-machine-sphere\">the Machine Sphere</a>, originally conceived for the Sons of Ether as a variant of Matter that would let them use their Primary Sphere to make the bulk of their Wonders. I have some concerns that this might undermine Utility too much and/or overpower the Field of Material Science, which is why I didn't include it here; but maybe I'm wrong?<br /> <br /> One of the notions here is that with a \u201cMachine Sphere\u201d, just like the Utility Sphere, the Quintessence that's used to make Wonders doesn't actually represent \u201cPrimal Energy\u201d; it would have to be an appropriate kind of Tass: an \u201cunobtanium\u201d special material which is defined as having the necessary exotic properties to make the Wonder work. The Quintessence rating of the Tass would be an abstract measure of how well the substance facilitates the Wonder's intended function. In effect, how much utility does the Tass provide to the Wonder? (Utility doesn't have to be <i>economic</i> utility.)<br /> <br /> 2. I've been going back and forth as to whether the \u201ctangible Prime stuff\u201d should go in Void or Energy. If I put it in Energy, I could also see putting Primal Energy there as well. That would certainly make up for the Energy Field's loss of motion and gravity as purviews; but I'm worried that it might go too far the other way. I also tend to think that the whole \u201cPrimal Energy\u201d thing isn't really a Technocratic thing, and was put into earlier Technocracy books due mainly to a lack of any better ideas; it was, at the time, the \u201cleast bad\u201d translation of the concept of Quintessence into the Technocratic paradigm. The ideas behind Primal Utility are arguably better. But again, I may be wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T22:23:20-07:00","id":1386007,"title":"","content":"I think I'm going to stick to the notion of folding those elements of Prime that don't fit Utility into Void. The Doylean rationale is that I don't want Energy to be the Field used for <i>ex nihilo</i> Effects, mainly because Energy is one of three Fields that gets <i>paired up with</i> another Field of you want to make something out of nothing (the other two being the counterparts to Life and Matter). <br /> <br /> The Watsonian rationale is that the Conventions see Void (or Dimensional Science) as a Field that deals with the fundamental structure of reality, with all the business about the Gauntlet and the Umbrae being a case of pockets of reality that are sectioned off from the primary reality of Conventional Space. In that view of things, Ephemera and Primal Energy are variations on a common theme: Primal Energy is to Conventional Space as Ephemera are to the Umbrae, and Ephemera is what Primal Energy becomes when it's cut off from the material world for too long. <br /> <br /> So in that regard, Void deals not just with the discarded realities of the Umbrae, but also with the primary reality of the physical world. It is in the context of \u201cdealing with the fundamental structure of the physical world\u201d that the stuff ported in from Prime comes into play. <br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-16-2020, 03:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T20:23:48-08:00","id":1526649,"title":"","content":"Here's a \u201cfirst draft\u201d of the Data Field:<br /> <br /> <u><b>Data (Information Science)</b></u><br /> This Field deals with formal sciences ranging from mathematics and logic to linguistics and information science. It provides the ability to detect and manipulate probabilities, and to access and manipulate all things digital. It can also cause changes to other information media, such the information being transmitted in radio signals and the words and images in a book \u2014 though for now, the latter is still firmly in the realm of Hypertech. In the Digital Web, it can be used just like Space. <br /> <br /> Data is often used in conjunction with Space for physical travel into the Digital Web (using a combination of Data's Web Access and Space's teleportation or portal effects), and with other Fields to extend their effects to reach subjects that aren't physically present. <br /> <br /> <b>Rank One Effects: </b><br /> \u2022 <i>Sense Connection: </i>the Scientist can detect effects utilizing Data to bypass distance. <br /> \u2022 <i>Analyze Chance:</i> as per Entropy. <br /> \u2022 <i>Decrypt:</i> as per Entropy. <br /> \u2022 <i>Nonlinear Prediction: </i>as per Entropy. <br /> \u2022 <i>Ring of Truth:</i> as per Entropy. <br /> \u2022 <i>Detect Digital Activity:</i> as per Mind's Detect Thoughts, but for data processing machinery. <br /> \u2022 <i>Mind Mapping: </i>the Scientist can run programs in his head, such as spreadsheets and databases. The number of successes required depends on how elaborate the programs are. <br /> <br /> <b>Rank Two Effects:</b><br /> \u2022 <i>Remote Viewing: </i>like Correspondence Sensing. <br /> \u2022 <i>Mask Signature:</i> the Scientist can hide his use of Data from those using Sense Connection to detect it. <br /> \u2022 <i>Web Access: </i>A successful use of this Adjustment allows the Scientist to mentally enter the Digital Web in a form of Astral Immersion (M20 p.467). Where M20 \u201crequires good VR equipment\u201d and \u201can Intelligence + Computer roll (three successes, difficulty 7)\u201d along with two dots of Correspondence, these rules treat it as a standard use of Enlightened Science, with the equipment requirements replaced by an appropriate Instrument such as Computers and IT Gear (M20 p.590) or Internet Activity (<b>Book of Secrets</b> pp.208\u2013209), and the Intelligence + Computer roll being replaced by Abilities Enhancing Magick (M20 p.533). This effect is a Simple Feat, only requiring a single success; though additional successes may be needed to extend the duration. Adding Space \u2022\u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 to the effect allows for Holistic Immersion instead: again, this is treated as an Enlightened Science Procedure, replacing the rules given on M20 p.467 with the usual \u201cget the right Instruments, engage an appropriate Practice, and get enough successes on an Enlightenment roll\u201d rules common to all Enlightened Science Procedures. <br /> \u2022 <i>Beginner's Luck:</i> as per Entropy. <br /> \u2022 <i>Fortune's Protection: </i>as per Entropy.<br /> \u2022 <i>Games of Luck:</i> as per Entropy.<br /> \u2022 <i>Firewall:</i> as per the Rank Two version of Mind's \u201cMind Shield\u201d effect, but shields data processing devices instead of minds. <br /> \u2022 <i>Networking: </i>as per Mind's Rank Three \u201cMental Networking\u201d effect, but for data manipulation gear. In conjunction with Mind \u2022\u2022\u2022, \u201cmachine minds\u201d and living minds can be networked together. <br /> \u2022 <i>Call Memophore: </i>as per Spirit's \u201cCall Spirit\u201d, but for Digital Web Entities (M20 pp.638\u2013639). <br /> <br /> <b>Rank Three Effects:</b><br /> \u2022 <i>Chain: </i>as per Correspondence. <br /> \u2022 <i>Fake activity: </i>as per the Rank Three version of Mind's \u201cFalse Thoughts\u201d, but for data processing machinery. <br /> \u2022 <i>Cunning Linguist:</i> as per Mind. <br /> \u2022 <i>Sensor Spoofing:</i> as per Mind's \u201cIllusory Input\u201d, but for sensory devices. <br /> \u2022 <i>Probe Activity: </i>as per Mind's \u201cProbe Thoughts\u201d, but for data processing devices. <br /> \u2022 <i>Denial of Service: </i>as per Mind's \u201cPsychic Assault\u201d, but for data processing devices. <br /> \u2022 <i>Technopathy: </i>as per Mind's \u201cTelepathy\u201d, but for data processing devices. <br /> \u2022 <i>Harm Memophore: </i>as per Spirit's \u201cHarm Spirit\u201d, but for Digital Web Entities. <br /> \u2022 <i>Heal Memophore: </i>as per Spirit's \u201cHeal Spirit\u201d, but for Digital Web Entities. <br /> <br /> <b>Rank Four Effects:</b><br /> \u2022 <i>Alter Memory: </i>as per Mind's \u201cManipulate Memory\u201d, but for data storage media. Among other things, this is what lets you alter the words on a page. <br /> \u2022 <i>Control Memophore: </i>as per Spirit's \u201cControl Spirit\u201d, but for Digital Web Entities. <br /> <br /> <b>Rank Five Effects:</b><br /> \u2022 <i>Probable Cause:</i> as per Entropy.<br /> \u2022 <i>Forge Memophore: </i>as per Spirit's \u201cForge Spirit\u201d, but for Digital Web Entities. <br /> <br /> <b>Data Connections:</b><br /> The rules for using Data to establish remote connections are the same as for Correspondence, with the caveat that if the subject isn't online, he's beyond Data's reach. The Correspondence Range table gets expanded to include more ways of establishment a connection to the subject: <br /> <br /> \u2022 Subject's presence or body sample; source code; government ID database information<br /> \u2022\u2022 A treasured possession or intimate companion, sample code, personal email or social media account. <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Casual possession or associate, legacy code, Internet stock puppet, throwaway email or media account. <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Acquaintance of or item from subject, derivative code, IP address. <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Operator briefly touched or meet subject, code from same language, rerouted IP string. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T11:36:30-07:00","id":1538665,"title":"","content":"Hello Dataweaver, thank you for inviting me here. I've read some of your first post, I haven't read it all nor the answers to it, I'll do in a few moments, but first I want to add a few scientific definitions and perhaps some preliminary thoughts, just in order to create a guide that may serve as a pillar to order our thoughts. &quot;Void&quot; and &quot;Utility&quot;, being more &quot;arcane&quot; Spheres, probably won't have &quot;scientific&quot; descriptions, but I'll try to come up with the best possible from philosophy or even pseudoscience if no better source can be find.<br /> <br /> I'll be editing this comment for a while, so just stick with me for a little:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>ENERGY</b><br /> <br /> <i>The word \u201cenergy\u201d comes from the Greek en\u00e9rgeia. Developed by Aristotle, en\u00e9rgeia has no direct translation to English. It is frequently described as \u201cbeing at work\u201d.</i> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What is energy?<br /> Scientists define energy as the <u><i>ability to do work</i></u>.<br /> <br /> There are many forms of energy:<br /> \u2022 Heat<br /> \u2022 Light<br /> \u2022 Motion<br /> \u2022 Electrical<br /> \u2022 Chemical<br /> \u2022 Gravitational<br /> \u2022 Nuclear<br /> <br /> These forms of energy can be grouped into two general types of energy for doing work:<br /> - Potential, or stored, energy<br /> - Kinetic, or working, energy<br /> <br /> <i>Source - U.S. Energy Information Administration (EIA) - <a href=\"https://www.eia.gov\" target=\"_blank\">www.eia.gov</a></i> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Work</b>, in <a href=\"https://www.britannica.com/science/physics-science\" target=\"_blank\">physics</a>, measure of <a href=\"https://www.britannica.com/science/energy\" target=\"_blank\">energy</a> transfer that occurs when an object is moved over a distance by an external <a href=\"https://www.britannica.com/science/force-physics\" target=\"_blank\">force</a> at least part of which is applied in the direction of the <a href=\"https://www.britannica.com/science/displacement-mechanics\" target=\"_blank\">displacement</a>.<br /> <br /> <i>Source: <a href=\"https://www.britannica.com/science/work-physics\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.britannica.com/science/work-physics</a></i> </div> </div> </div>So, very well. All of this is for us to understand that in science, Energy deals with everything that either causes or has the potential to cause MOVEMENT.<br /> <br /> Everything about energy is related to movement in one way or another; everything in the universe is in constant movement; we could even say that the universe &quot;vibrates&quot; down to it sub atomic level (the String theory of physics deals exactly with that prospect, although... Well, let's not go into that bag of worms for now, because as it stands, String theory may end up becoming the Relativity of the 21th century, or the &quot;universal Ether&quot; equivalent of failed theory, so let's keep that aside for now).<br /> <br /> &quot;Movement&quot; is <u>Kinetic energy</u>; it's energy creating &quot;work&quot; (work here in physical terms, aka the movement of something across space) over a macro scale.<br /> <br /> &quot;<u>Light</u>&quot; is the movement of the subatomic particles known as photons.<br /> <br /> &quot;<u>Heat</u>&quot; is the vibrational movement at a molecular scale. The more intensity in the vibration of molecules, the higher the heat<br /> <br /> &quot;Nuclear&quot; energy is a bit more complex. There are actually two &quot;nuclear&quot; forces, the strong and the weak.<br /> <br /> The <u>strong nuclear force</u> is responsible for keeping atoms together. Atoms are made of a nucleus that has protons and neutrons bound together, with electrons orbiting that nucleus.<br /> <br /> Very well. But Protons and Neutrons are all made of a combination of 3 particles each, known as <i>Quarks.</i> So, each Proton or Neutron is composed of 3 Quarks; the types of Quarks will define if the result will be a Proton or Neutron.<br /> <br /> The force that thus keeps those Quarks together is the Strong Nuclear Force. That Force is also responsible for keeping the Protons and Neutrons &quot;glued&quot; together inside of the nucleus of the Atom.<br /> <br /> The <u>weak nuclear force</u> is the one responsible for the radioactive decay of particles.<br /> <br /> And yes, those two forces are what fission or fusion liberates as energy.<br /> <br /> <u>Gravitational energy</u> is an energy that comes from anything that has mass; most of everything in the universe has mass, even most subatomic particles, so most of everything has gravity - but there actually are exceptions. Photons, for instance, the very same particles that carry light energy, DON'T have mass, and therefore, have no Gravity.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<u>Electrical energy</u> is the power an atom's charged particles have to cause an action or move an object. The movement of electrons from one atom to another is what results in electrical energy.<br /> <br /> Now, in here I think it's important to talk about the 4 fundamental physical Forces:<br /> - Strong Nuclear Force;<br /> - Electromagnetism;<br /> - Weak Nuclear Force;<br /> - Gravity<br /> <br /> And I purposefully ordered them from strongest to weakest.<br /> <br /> But why is gravity the weakest if it is capable of moving galaxies?<br /> <br /> Well, the strong and weak nuclear forces have a very short range; basically, they only affect stuff inside of the atom and not beyond.<br /> <br /> Electromagnetism is far stronger than Gravity (that's easy to attest, a small magnet is capable of attracting a clip and thus beat the gravity of the entire Earth), but the reason to why it doesn't move galaxies is because there are the same quantity of electrically charged particles positive as there are negative, so they cancel each others out.<br /> <br /> And thus, despite Gravity being the weakest, it affects everything because it has long range (the entire universe actually) and is not cancelled by an opposing force.<br /> <br /> Now I must discuss a bit about <i>chemical energy</i>, and that's a bit trickier. Because that's NOT a source of &quot;energy&quot; that comes from physics, but rather from chemistry.<br /> <br /> <u>Chemical energy</u> is present in atomic interactions in a &quot;potential&quot; form. There are 3 forms of atomic interactions upon which different atoms &quot;bind&quot; together (forgive me, but I don't know all the proper names in English). Those are:<br /> - Metallic;<br /> - Ionic and<br /> - Molecular<br /> <br /> &quot;Metallic&quot; refers to the characteristic of certain elements to be &quot;negatively charged&quot;... Hmmm... That's a... Bit complex to explain, but I'll try in a very simple way.<br /> <br /> But... I'm afraid we'll have to go to the very beginning...<br /> <br /> So, an &quot;atom&quot; is the smallest component of matter. Kind of... There are &quot;subatomic particles&quot; but... That's another story...<br /> <br /> So, atoms have basically 3 components, protons, which are charged positively, neutrons, which have neutral (&quot;zero&quot;) charge, and serve basically to keep the protons &quot;glued&quot; inside the nucleus, and electrons which are charged negative and orbit the nucleus in constant movement.<br /> <br /> What defines one element from another is the amount of protons it has in the nucleus. So, the most common element in the universe is Hidrogen, with just a single proton. The second most common is Helium, with 2 protons.<br /> <br /> That's what defines the period table. Each one of the elements there has a different amount of protons, from 1 (Hidrogen) to the hypothetical artificial ones (with hundreds).<br /> <br /> So, Carbon for example has 14 protons, and so on.<br /> <br /> There is a complication thou about how the electrons orbit the nucleus of an atom; each electron has 1 negative charge and each Proton, 1 positive, and they cancel each other.<br /> <br /> Positive attracts negative, thus an atom of Carbon should attract 14 electrons.<br /> <br /> However, since all electrons are negative, they REPEL each other, and thus they don't all orbit the nucleus in the same way, but rather in LAYERS.<br /> <br /> And there's a specific distribution for that (which I won't get into right now), but on every atom, the last layer can only ever have a max of 8 electrons.<br /> <br /> Now, atoms that have either 2 or 8 electrons in the last layer are highly stable and will NEVER combine with anything, so much so that on Earth you'll never find them on any state but as gas; it's the so called &quot;Noble Gases&quot;, like Helium or Argonium - remember when I said that Helium has 2 protons? Well, that means that it has 2 electrons, thus it has only a single layer of electrons, and that layer has exactly 2 electrons, meaning that this is a stable atom.<br /> <br /> Hidrogen, on the other hand, only has a single electron. This means that, in order for it to become stable, the Hidrogen needs to &quot;borrow&quot; an electron from another atom, thus getting is electron layer stable with 2.<br /> <br /> In chemistry, we say therefore that Hidrogen has a &quot;1 positive charge&quot;, because it has a tendency to &quot;snatch&quot; 1 electron.<br /> <br /> The family of elements known as &quot;metals&quot;, however, have &quot;negative charges&quot; because they have a tendency to &quot;expell&quot; electrons from their electron cloud. Such is the case of any elements with 3 electrons in their last layer for example, which will have the tendency to expell one of theirs in order to become stable with 1.<br /> <br /> Metallic interactions are thus formed by those metallic elements. In a metallic interaction, all the atoms are, roughly saying, constantly &quot;pushing&quot; electrons between each other. The electrons are running wild between metals, which is why this is the strongest interaction. It's also why metals can conduct electricity - the electrons &quot;travel freely&quot; inside of them.<br /> <br /> Them comes the <u>Ionic interactions</u>, which are the interactions of atoms with positive and negative charges (aka atoms that &quot;snatch&quot; and &quot;repel&quot; electrons). The most familiar to us is common Salt, which is an atom of Na (Sodium, Na is from the name in Latin) and Cl (chlorine? Damn, I don't know the name in English, sorry). Anyway, Na has 1 positive charge (it attracts 1 electron) and Cl has 1 negative charge (it repels 1 electron).<br /> <br /> Because of that, they form a very strong ionic interaction between one another (salt dissolves in water because water, H2O, actually becomes dissociated into H+ and OH- ions, which will attract the Cl and Na ions from salt respectively)<br /> <br /> And the last one is the <u>molecular interaction</u> which is the weakest of the 3 (but still very strong - our bodies are made of molecules after all), which is the interactions between positively charged atoms.<br /> <br /> Our most basic components - Hidrogen, Oxygen, Carbon and Nitrogen - are all positively charged, thus they form molecular bounds easily<br /> <br /> <br /> WELL...<br /> <br /> What happens is that not all atomic interactions are born equal; some are stronger than other, more stable than others.<br /> <br /> And external energy can break those bonds. That's the whole thing we call as &quot;chemistry&quot;. Chemistry is, essentially, the study of the bonds between atoms.<br /> <br /> So, for instance, a molecule of Oxygen is made up of 2 atoms of Oxygen (O2).<br /> <br /> However, if you bombard the Oxygen molecules with energy (say, for instance, photons coming from the Sun), they may break up and form Ozone instead, which are molecules made of a trio of Oxygen atoms (O3) with a highly energetic and unstable interaction.<br /> <br /> Now, nature always tends from &quot;unstable&quot; to &quot;stable&quot;, but it is possible to move in the other direction by application of energy; with enough heat for example, you can undo even the metallic interactions.<br /> <br /> So, Ozone for example has &quot;chemical energy&quot; stored in the form of unstable interaction between atoms. If another molecule that is more stable than Ozone and that has affinity towards it passes by, it can break the Ozone and &quot;steal&quot; that energy away.<br /> <br /> Biochemical processes make use of that all the time. Sugar (Glucose, C6H12O6, meaning 6 atoms of carbon, 12 of Hidrogen and 6 of Oxygen) is the main source of &quot;energy&quot; for most living beings. That &quot;energy&quot; comes from the dissociation of this large molecule, either into alcohol by bacteria that doesn't use Oxygen (alcohol is C2H6O) or CO2 and water for all others that breath oxygen.<br /> <br /> The extra energy that was stored in the glucose molecules is used for all the metabolic process of the living beings, used to build other kinds of molecules or for movement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","user":"Magus Maximus","date":". 07-16-2024, 04:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T11:59:54-07:00","id":1538666,"title":"","content":"You might also want to look at the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/428316-the-machine-sphere\">Machine Sphere</a>, which I'm thinking of borrowing from for the Field of Matter. In particular, I like the inclusion of mechanisms as a Matter parallel to Life's organisms.<br /> <br /> Also, don't be shy about suggesting alternate names when you think they're appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":".  Added note 07-16-2024, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T13:09:13-07:00","id":1538671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385360-fields-for-the-technocracy-reloaded?p=1385370#post1385370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. I had originally been thinking of doing something like <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/428316-the-machine-sphere\">the Machine Sphere</a>, originally conceived for the Sons of Ether as a variant of Matter that would let them use their Primary Sphere to make the bulk of their Wonders. I have some concerns that this might undermine Utility too much and/or overpower the Field of Material Science, which is why I didn't include it here; but maybe I'm wrong?.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Machine still needs a huge amount of Quintessence to do it's thing, and the Syndicate business models (PU) &quot;powering&quot; ItX industry (Machine) it's very &quot;on brand&quot; for the whole Technocratic division of labour<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Utility it's a very powerful Sphere, while not able to create &quot;out of nothing&quot;, it has a lot easier time gathering energy, and it has a sort of &quot;social power&quot; that comes from the association of Utility with the success of business and the distribution of wealth - which it's, to me, a little hard to measure.<br /> <br /> I've been thinking if PU shouldn't have some elements of &quot;Fate&quot;.<br /> <br /> Like, the books really stress out that &quot;utility&quot; it's related to economical &quot;success&quot;, in ways that are very &quot;entropy blessing like&quot; to me. Like how harvesting too much juice from business it's very bad for the business (implying putting energy in should be good) - but how this collapse or rise happens it's not very specific.<br /> <br /> Perhaps one could have a distiction between &quot;deterministic&quot; and &quot;non-deterministic&quot; factors. Data can manipulate/determine the probability of a building collapsing - modified by the actual &quot;real-state&quot; of the building. PU, instead, can determine if the building it's going to have a promissing future or not, but you don't know anything about it w/o further Fields.<br /> <br /> This could cover some of the effects of Entropy where you just give non-specific &quot;good luck&quot; and &quot;bad luck&quot; - except that luck it's more of a sense about the importance of things, you don't know what's gonna happen, but you know when something it's useful as a sort of potential.<br /> <br /> And this actually could incorporate the Entropic concept of &quot;Decay&quot; better than just getting older: Decay as the loss of the Utility over time could define not just growing older, but specifically weaker. Consider - perhaps a bit cynically - the spread of systemic corruption as a &quot;loss of Utility&quot; that happens at a societal level, and then one can have a very clear picture of what's happening to the &quot;so-promissing venture&quot; that it's now &quot;inexplicably collapsing&quot; after you took the Utility from it<br /> <br /> However, I fear that this could make PU <i>too strong</i> ... and if I'm suggesting it at all it's because I have the felling that PU<i> already kinda does this </i>when you &quot;take away the Utility of a Venture&quot;, and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-16-2024, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T14:41:42-07:00","id":1538678,"title":"","content":"Phew... I ended up putting more than I anticipated. Sorry for being too prolific.<br /> <br /> I wanted to add something about &quot;Emergent Patterns&quot; but duty calls, I'll just leave it here so I don't forget.<br /> <br /> Also, I wanted to discuss Matter a bit, because I believe that for Techies, Transmutation should be Matter 4 or 5, because it is the hardest thing possible. To transmute elements, you need to modify the amount of protons in an atom, and that only happens inside of stars - and the heaviest elements are only ever created when a star goes supernova. I'll address those later on","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T19:49:39-07:00","id":1538693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385360-fields-for-the-technocracy-reloaded#post1385360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Data</i> draws Digital Web access and Sympathetic Connections from Correspondence, and manipulation of order and chaos from Entropy; it also gets effects for dealing with the manipulation of sensors and digital records that echo Mind Effects, and effects for summoning, binding and warding digital entities that echo Spirit Effects. It also gets the \u201cspatial manipulation\u201d stuff from Correspondence, but <i>only</i> in the context of the Digital Web: that is, it can teleport, create gateways, co-locate, etc., just like Correspondence can, but <i>only</i> in the Digital Web. This is different from the Data Sphere variant described in M20, drastically limiting its Correspondence-related capabilities, and is the reason why I'm okay with it having so many other capabilities derived from Entropy, Mind, and Spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Fields don't have an Entropy equivalent because Enlightened Science doesn't really work that way. Manipulation of order and chaos went to Data by thinking of them as identifying and manipulating small-p patterns, while the death and decay stuff went to Time mainly to bolster it; but thinking of it in terms of age manipulation works reasonably well. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most if not all of these Fields have parallels to branches of science: Energy, Space, and Time together represent physics; Matter covers chemistry and mechanics; Life covers most of the Life Sciences (though ecology might require some Data to deal with the intricate networks of interactions between different lifeforms). Data is all about the formal sciences: logic, mathematics, computer science, linguistics, etc. Mind is all about the bulk of the social sciences, save only for economics which is handled by Utility. </div> </div> </div>Well, I absolutely love Entropy but...<br /> <br /> I like the idea of &quot;Data&quot;. May I make you a tiny suggestion thou?<br /> <br /> How about rebranding it to &quot;Information&quot;?<br /> <br /> And there's a reason and method for this.<br /> <br /> You see, the idea of &quot;Information&quot; has become a central tenet in physics. Modern physics actually sees the universe in terms of &quot;Information&quot; rather than anything else.<br /> <br /> And let's be honest, nothing more Sci Fi and techie boy hardcore than that.<br /> <br /> Sure, physics has its own definition of &quot;information&quot; which is as follows:","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T20:16:01-07:00","id":1538694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Big Think</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Why information is central to physics and the universe itself</b><br /> Information may not seem like something physical, yet it has become a central concern for physicists. A wonderful new book explores the importance of the \u201cdataome\u201d for the physical, biological, and human worlds...</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The most important current topic in physics relates to a subject that hardly seems physical at all \u2014 information, which is central to thermodynamics and perhaps the universe itself. The \u201cdataome\u201d is the way human beings have been externalizing information about ourselves and the world since we first began making paintings on cave walls. The dataome is vast and growing everyday, sucking up an ever increasing share of the energy humans produce. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Physics is a field that is supposed to study real stuff. By real, I mean things like matter and energy. Matter is, of course, the kind of stuff you can hold in your hand. Energy may seem a little more abstract, but its reality is pretty apparent, appearing in the form of motion or gravity or electromagnetic fields.<br /> What has become apparent recently, however, is the importance to physics of something that seems somewhat less real: information. From black holes to quantum mechanics to understanding the physics of life, information has risen to become a principal concern of many physicists in many domains. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What is the dataome?<br /> In his new book, Scharf is seeking a deeper understanding of what he calls the \u201cdataome.\u201d This is the way human beings have been externalizing information about ourselves and the world since we first began making paintings on cave walls. The book opens with a compelling exploration of how Shakespeare\u2019s works, which began as scribbles on a page, have gone on to have lives of their own in the dataome. Through reprintings in different languages, recordings of performances, movie adaptations, comic books, and so on, Shakespeare\u2019s works are now a permanent part of the vast swirling ensemble of information that constitutes the human dataome. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the dataome does not just live in our heads. Scharf takes us on a proper physicist\u2019s journey through the dataome, showing us how information can never be divorced from energy. Your brain needs the chemical energy from food you ate this morning to read, process, and interpret these words. One of the most engaging parts of the book is when Scharf details just how much energy and real physical space our data-hungry world consumes as it adds to the dataome. For example, the <a href=\"https://technologymagazine.com/top10/top-10-biggest-data-centres-world/china-telecom-data-centre-china\" target=\"_blank\">Hohhot Data Center</a> in the Inner Mongolia Autonomous Region of China is made of vast \u201cfarms\u201d of data processing servers covering 245 acres of real estate. A single application like Bitcoin, Scharf tells us, consumes 7.7 gigawatts per year, equivalent to the output of half a dozen nuclear reactors! </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the dataome is not just about energy. Entropy is central to the story as well. Scharf takes the reader through a beautifully crafted discussion of information and the science of thermodynamics. This is where the links between energy, entropy, the limits of useful work, and probability all become profoundly connected to the definition of information. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The second law of thermodynamics tells us that you <i>cannot</i> use all of a given amount of energy to do useful work. Some of that energy must be wasted by getting turned into heat. Entropy is the physicist\u2019s way of measuring that waste (which can also be thought of as disorder). Scharf takes the reader through the basic relations of thermodynamics and then shows how entropy became intimately linked with information. It was <a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?client=safari&amp;rls=en&amp;q=Claude+Shannon%E2%80%99s&amp;ie=UTF-8&amp;oe=UTF-8\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Shannon\u2019s</a> brilliant work in the 1940s that showed how information \u2014 bits \u2014 could be defined for communication and computation as an entropy associated with the redundancy of strings of symbols. That was the link tying the physical world of physics explicitly to the informational and computational world of the dataome.\u200b </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The best parts of the book are where Scharf unpacks how information makes its appearance in biology. From the data storage and processing that occurs with every strand of DNA, to the tangled pathways that define evolutionary dynamics, Scharf demonstrates how life is what happens to physics and chemistry when information matters. </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://bigthink.com/13-8/information-central-physics-universe/\" target=\"_blank\">https://bigthink.com/13-8/informatio...sics-universe/</a><br /> <br /> Now, maybe you've heard that &quot;information cannot travel faster than the speed of light&quot;, or perhaps even heard about the law of &quot;conservation of information&quot;. There's even some crazy stuff about something called the &quot;Holographic Principle&quot;, upon which our entire 3D universe may simply be some &quot;encoded&quot; (informational) &quot;hologram&quot; projected in a 2D reality.<br /> <br /> Yeah. No, I won't go much deeper in that Marauder rabbit hole here.<br /> <br /> Regardless, modern physics now take &quot;Information&quot; as something VERY serious and not just an abstract concept, and what's more, it is a CORE PILLAR OF REALITY ITSELF.<br /> <br /> But what exactly is &quot;Information&quot; for physics, and how could we translate that for Mage (Either as Data or Information Sphere)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T20:50:35-07:00","id":1538695,"title":"","content":"Now, the idea of &quot;information&quot; inside of physics is a bit complex, so I decided to get the help of ChatGPT to help me translate it in the best way possible. Here is the transcript:<br /> <br /> <b>Me:</b> What is the definition of Information in physics?<br /> <b>GPT:</b> In physics, information can be defined as a measure of the degree of randomness or disorder in a system. It is often associated with the amount of uncertainty or surprise in an event or a message. Information theory, developed by Claude Shannon, deals with quantifying information and how it can be transmitted efficiently over communication channels. This theory provides a framework for understanding how information is encoded, transmitted, and decoded accurately.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Me:</b> But why information can't go faster than light and what is its relation to the rest of physics?<br /> <b>GPT:</b> In physics, information cannot travel faster than light because of the fundamental principles of relativity, specifically Einstein's theory of special relativity. According to this theory, the speed of light in a vacuum is the ultimate speed limit in the universe. Anything that has mass would require an infinite amount of energy to reach or exceed the speed of light, which is physically impossible.<br /> The limitation imposed by the speed of light has profound implications for information transmission. If information could travel faster than light, it would violate causality, leading to paradoxes like effect preceding cause in certain reference frames.<br /> <br /> The relationship between information and the rest of physics is intricate. Information theory provides insights into how information is processed, stored, and transmitted in physical systems. It has applications in various fields like quantum mechanics, thermodynamics, and even black hole physics.<br /> <br /> Quantum mechanics, for instance, explores how information is encoded in quantum states and how it behaves differently from classical information. In thermodynamics, concepts like entropy and information play crucial roles in understanding the flow of heat and energy in systems. Even in black hole physics, the idea of black hole entropy relates to the amount of information that can be stored on its event horizon.<br /> <br /> Overall, the study of information in physics bridges different disciplines and offers a deeper understanding of how the universe operates at a fundamental level.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Me:</b> What is the law of &quot;conservation of information&quot; in physics?<br /> <b>GPT: </b>The concept of the &quot;conservation of information&quot; in physics is not a well-established law like the conservation of energy or momentum. However, it is a topic that arises in discussions related to quantum mechanics, black hole physics, and information theory.<br /> <br /> In the context of quantum mechanics, the conservation of information refers to the idea that information cannot be lost or destroyed in a closed quantum system. This principle is closely related to the concept of unitarity, which states that the evolution of a quantum system must be reversible and preserve information.<br /> <br /> In the study of black holes, the conservation of information is a significant puzzle known as the &quot;black hole information paradox.&quot; This paradox arises from the conflict between general relativity and quantum mechanics regarding what happens to information that falls into a black hole. According to quantum mechanics, information must be conserved, but general relativity suggests that information could be lost when it falls into a black hole.<br /> <br /> Efforts to resolve this paradox have led to new insights into the nature of space, time, and information. The idea that information cannot be lost challenges our understanding of fundamental physical principles and has implications for how we perceive the universe at both macroscopic and microscopic scales.<br /> <br /> In summary, while the conservation of information may not be a strict law like other conservation principles in physics, it is a concept that plays a crucial role in understanding quantum mechanics, black hole physics, and the nature of information itself.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Me:</b> What is information in a black hole?<br /> <b>GPT: </b>Within the physics of black holes, the issue of information is a fascinating and complex topic. According to classical physics, when matter falls into a black hole, all the information contained in that matter would be lost forever, which would conflict with the principles of quantum mechanics, stating that information cannot be destroyed. <br /> The idea that information cannot be lost has led to the formulation of the black hole information paradox. This paradox questions what happens to the information when it crosses the event horizon of a black hole and is sucked in.<br /> <br /> One proposed solution to this paradox is the &quot;complementarity hypothesis,&quot; suggested by Leonard Susskind and other physicists. This hypothesis posits that from the perspective of an observer outside the black hole, information is preserved and can eventually be recovered. However, from the viewpoint of an observer crossing the event horizon and falling into the black hole, the information is indeed lost.<br /> <br /> Another important proposal is the idea that information is encoded in the Hawking radiation emitted by black holes. This radiation contains traces of the information that fell into the black hole, suggesting that the information is not truly lost but rather encoded in a subtle way.<br /> <br /> In summary, the issue of information in black holes raises profound questions about the limits of current physics and challenges our understanding of the nature of information and its preservation under extreme conditions such as those found in black holes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Me:</b> What does it mean &quot;information contained in matter&quot;?<br /> <b>GPT:</b> The concept of &quot;information contained in matter&quot; refers to the idea that the arrangement and properties of particles or systems of particles carry information about their past, present, and potential future states. In a broader sense, this information encompasses all the characteristics, interactions, and histories of the particles that make up a physical system.<br /> <br /> In the context of black holes, when matter falls into a black hole, it carries with it various forms of information such as its mass, energy, momentum, spin, and other quantum properties. According to quantum mechanics, this information is encoded in the quantum state of the matter particles.<br /> <br /> The preservation of this information is crucial for maintaining consistency with fundamental principles of physics, such as unitarity and reversibility. If information were truly lost when matter falls into a black hole, it would violate these principles and challenge our understanding of how physical systems evolve over time.<br /> <br /> Therefore, the notion of &quot;information contained in matter&quot; highlights the idea that every physical system carries a wealth of information that characterizes its behavior and evolution, and preserving this information is essential for understanding the dynamics of the universe at both macroscopic and microscopic scales.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T20:51:44-07:00","id":1538696,"title":"","content":"There are four names in this set that aren't negotiable, because they're linked to existing material: <br /> <br /> Data, Dimensional Science, Primal Utility, and Void Correspondence. Data first appeared in <b>NWO Convention Book</b>; Dimensional Science first appeared in <b>Technocracy: Void Engineers</b>; Primal Utility first appeared in <b>Syndicate Convention Book</b>; and Void Correspondence has <i>only</i> appeared in <b>Void Engineers Convention Book</b>. <br /> <br /> I'm giving each Field a one-word name and a two-word name; the former being for \u201cHuffman Encoding\u201d (names that are frequently used should be short), and the latter being for flavor. The \u201cshort name\u201d thing is why Dimensional Science is also called Void; why Primal Utility is also called Utility; and why Void Correspondence is also called Space. <br /> <br /> With Data, it's the other way around: Data is perfect as a short name; so I gave it a more flavorful long name. Notice what it is? Yep; <i>Information</i> Science. Because I agree with you: in many ways, Information <i>is </i>a better name for it. But because I'm trying to maintain a connection to the original Sphere variants that I took inspiration from, I can't use Information as the short name. <br /> <br /> The other fourteen names (eight short and six long) are subject to negotiation. If you can think of a better short name for Void Utility than Utility, for instance, I'm all ears. (I'm half-inclined to suggest \u201cPower\u201d, used in the sense of \u201cthe ability to be and to make things be\u201d \u2014 especially if we shift the Field from being purely about economics to being about socio-economics and politics \u2014 but that's probably too easy to get mixed up with Energy.) Both Matter and Material Science are subject to revision if better options are presented; for instance, I'm strongly inclined to somehow use Mechanics and Organics in the Field names corresponding to Matter and Life; though I'm not sure if I want them as the short names or as part of the long names. And so on. But Data, Dimensional Science, Primal Utility, and Void Correspondence aren't going to change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T21:05:19-07:00","id":1538697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385360-fields-for-the-technocracy-reloaded?p=1538678#post1538678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Phew... I ended up putting more than I anticipated. Sorry for being too prolific.<br /> <br /> I wanted to add something about &quot;Emergent Patterns&quot; but duty calls, I'll just leave it here so I don't forget.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm looking forward to part two. Also, thinks for the rundown on Information: I was vaguely aware of it before; but it firmly cements my decision to include much of the Entropy Sphere in the Data Field. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385360-fields-for-the-technocracy-reloaded?p=1538678#post1538678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I wanted to discuss Matter a bit, because I believe that for Techies, Transmutation should be Matter 4 or 5, because it is the hardest thing possible. To transmute elements, you need to modify the amount of protons in an atom, and that only happens inside of stars - and the heaviest elements are only ever created when a star goes supernova. I'll address those later on</div> </div> </div> </div>Consider the possibility that chemical and nuclear transformations might both require Conjunctional use of Energy and Matter, because both are nearly always either endothermic or exothermic, with the former turning energy into matter while the latter turns matter into energy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T21:20:54-07:00","id":1538698,"title":"","content":"Now, I bet most people here already heard about &quot;Schrodinger's cat&quot; and some other absurdities of quantum physics, but I myself adhere to the theory of &quot;Superdeterminism&quot; that eliminates most of the ocus pocus sorcery of quantum mechanics; that's not particularly important however.<br /> <br /> What's important is that the universe is a deterministic system, which means that everything is based on a sequence of cause and effect (hence why I'm a &quot;materialist mechanicist&quot;). And the &quot;information&quot; on any system is reversible. This means that, if you get any set of particles and ALWAYS have the SAME amounts of momentum, energy, mass, spin and any other quantum characteristics, if you repeat those exact values an infinite amount of times, they'll behave in the exact same manner an infinite amount of times.<br /> <br /> This means that any &quot;Information&quot; inside of any (and actually ALL) particles in the Universe is preserved in fact from the very beginning of the Universe... But also up to its very end.<br /> <br /> Yes, that's right. The Universe is like a book that has already been written, and all of its history is engraved in a cosmic book. This is metaphor, but it is true: suppose we could build a super quantum computer bigger than the Universe itself, so powerful that it could actually calculate the momentum, mass, position, energy, spin and ALL other variables of EVERY SINGLE PARTICLE in the Universe.<br /> <br /> Then, that Supercomputer would be OMNISCIENT, because it would be able to calculate the past or the future of the entire Universe at any given point, because the Information of the Universe is preserved throughout all of the past, present and even future. You could, in theory, trace any particle in the Universe all the way back to the Big Bang or all the way down to the entropic heat death of the Universe.<br /> <br /> THIS is information. It's hard for me to explain, I can only (barely) visualize it.<br /> <br /> The interesting part of this is that, inside of a black hole, this seems to collapse. You cannot reverse quantum states from a black hole because apparently, all the information has been lost inside of it - meaning, it's impossible to know which particles went into the black hole, nor from which direction or when. This is... Insane. As if causality completely breaks inside one.<br /> <br /> It also appears that the information is conserved at the event horizon of black holes, but not after it. That's... Strange. Because time literally STOPS once you &quot;cross&quot; the event horizon (so you don't actually cross it, because you remain frozen in time for all eternity)... Black holes are weird because they lead to a bunch of results giving infinity, or something divided by zero, or infinity divided by zero, and thus math completely breaks after the event horizon, so... Who really knows. But information is still preserved at the event horizon nevertheless, forever frozen in time... But &quot;inside&quot; the Black Hole, which takes &quot;longer than eternity&quot; to get, is not... Yeah, don't try to understand. Even Einstein couldn't, so who am I to even try.<br /> <br /> There's some ideas involving Hawking radiation (which is radiation emanated veeeeeery slowly from Black Holes) that some physicists believe to give information back to the universe, and thus it is not really lost after all, but there's no consensus about it.<br /> <br /> <b><i><u>Ok kids, school is out. No more, I promise</u></i></b><br /> <br /> Very well. Back to business now, we may begin. I'm finally ready.<br /> <br /> PS: please, if I'm being pedantic and boring, just let me know, I won't be offended. I seriously prefer to know.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T21:28:36-07:00","id":1538699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385360-fields-for-the-technocracy-reloaded?p=1538671#post1538671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Machine still needs a huge amount of Quintessence to do it's thing, and the Syndicate business models (PU) &quot;powering&quot; ItX industry (Machine) it's very &quot;on brand&quot; for the whole Technocratic division of labour</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to agree. <i>If</i> the Matter Field ends up getting the ability to craft Wonders, it should be harder to do that than to use Utility for the task. And I'm thinking that the Matter Field shouldn't have that ability. That's why I said \u201ctake inspiration from\u201d, not \u201ccopy it verbatim\u201d. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385360-fields-for-the-technocracy-reloaded?p=1538671#post1538671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Utility it's a very powerful Sphere, while not able to create &quot;out of nothing&quot;, it has a lot easier time gathering energy, and it has a sort of &quot;social power&quot; that comes from the association of Utility with the success of business and the distribution of wealth - which it's, to me, a little hard to measure.<br /> <br /> I've been thinking if PU shouldn't have some elements of &quot;Fate&quot;.<br /> <br /> Like, the books really stress out that &quot;utility&quot; it's related to economical &quot;success&quot;, in ways that are very &quot;entropy blessing like&quot; to me. Like how harvesting too much juice from business it's very bad for the business (implying putting energy in should be good) - but how this collapse or rise happens it's not very specific.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. But note that the Utility version of this involves investing points of Primal Energy (or whatever it's called in the context of Utility) into the Venture that you want to bless; the Entropy version doesn't. Wherever the Entropy version ends up, its edge over the Utility version is that it doesn't cost PE to use it. <br /> <br /> With that said, I'm all for the idea of making PU into something broader than economics. I think the defining feature, and the thing borrowed from Entropy, is the ability to target <i>groups and organizations </i>with your Science, instead of targeting individuals. Want a Mind Effect to influence an entire stadium audience? Craft the Mind Effect as normal, then add a bit of PU to it in order to target the audience as of it were a single entity. <br /> <br /> That makes PU as much about sociology and politics as it is about money. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385360-fields-for-the-technocracy-reloaded?p=1538671#post1538671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this actually could incorporate the Entropic concept of &quot;Decay&quot; better than just getting older: Decay as the loss of the Utility over time could define not just growing older, but specifically weaker. Consider - perhaps a bit cynically - the spread of systemic corruption as a &quot;loss of Utility&quot; that happens at a societal level, and then one can have a very clear picture of what's happening to the &quot;so-promissing venture&quot; that it's now &quot;inexplicably collapsing&quot; after you took the Utility from it<br /> <br /> However, I fear that this could make PU <i>too strong</i> ... and if I'm suggesting it at all it's because I have the felling that PU<i> already kinda does this </i>when you &quot;take away the Utility of a Venture&quot;, and such.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah; I'm also worried that this would make PU too powerful. Likewise with trying to fold the decay stuff into Data, which is also getting massively boosted in this model; it doesn't need the <i>entire</i> Sphere of Entropy. I think I'll stick with the \u201cdecay\u201d stuff being folded into Time. Keeping in mind that it goes both ways: if the ability to use Time to make something old and decrepit, you also have the ability to use Time to make it young and vibrant. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T21:37:04-07:00","id":1538700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385360-fields-for-the-technocracy-reloaded?p=1538698#post1538698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">PS: please, if I'm being pedantic and boring, just let me know, I won't be offended. I seriously prefer to know.</div> </div> </div> </div>You did say that you're laying groundwork. Fair enough; and feel free to continue so long as you're laying groundwork. But at some point, I expect you to shift gears and start building on that groundwork. At that point, try to be less pedantic, and produce something practical for a TTRPG.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T22:15:43-07:00","id":1538703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385360-fields-for-the-technocracy-reloaded?p=1538697#post1538697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm looking forward to part two. Also, thinks for the rundown on Information: I was vaguely aware of it before; but it firmly cements my decision to include much of the Entropy Sphere in the Data Field.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. That's a relief. I was worried that I might have been inconvenient, and it is good to feel useful, so I appreciate.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Consider the possibility that chemical and nuclear transformations might both require Conjunctional use of Energy and Matter, because both are nearly always either endothermic or exothermic, with the former turning energy into matter while the latter turns matter into energy. </div> </div> </div>Yeah well, in a sense that much is true in a physical sense, but then we would get in a problem about how to divide the game mechanics in sensible &quot;packages&quot;. Because, if we go that way, then &quot;Biology&quot; is also just Chemistry (&quot;biochemistry&quot;, but that's just a specialization of chemistry) which then it's just actually how energy behaves; in the end, &quot;Matter&quot; is actually just &quot;solid energy&quot;. Atoms are made of Protons, that require particles like Quarks and gluons and neutrinos and whatnot, and many of those actually have ZERO mass, because what gives mass is a very specific particle called the &quot;Higgs Boson&quot;, thus many of those subatomic particles are actually PURE ENERGY, then if we go into String Theory, than everything gets even worse, because even deeper than those known particles, everything in the Universe would be literally just &quot;vibrating strings&quot;, pure energy, so there really is no matter at all, just energy in fact, vibrating in different frequencies thus creating different stuff...<br /> <br /> Thus we could just say that everything in the &quot;Frontline&quot; &quot;Material Plane&quot; is controlled by a single &quot;Uber Sphere&quot; (the &quot;Material Sphere&quot;?)<br /> <br /> Now, this actually ties up well to something that I already wanted to mention coincidentally. It's the phenomenon called &quot;Emergent Patterns&quot;. And that's the reason why the study of Physics is separated from Chemistry and those 2 from Biology, and that's also why we don't try to understand Psychology in terms of Quantum Physics.<br /> <br /> In a very succinct manner, Emergent Patterns means that &quot;the whole is bigger than the sum of its parts&quot;.<br /> <br /> Example: let's go full Jack the Ripper and &quot;disembowel&quot; a person with medical precision.<br /> <br /> Let's remove the brain, the spinal cord, the heart, liver, lungs, stomach, intestine, kidneys, muscles, bones and every other organ of a person - even preserving all blood and all fluids of him.<br /> <br /> Now, if I dump it all into a chest, will a human being come out of it?<br /> <br /> Of course not. Because a human being is more than just a sum of a bunch of organs.<br /> <br /> Likewise, if I disassemble all cells from somebody's eyes and then dump them into a petri dish, will I have an eye back?<br /> <br /> Obviously not.<br /> <br /> In the same manner, atoms are more than just a collection of protons and neutrons and electrons, and molecules are more than just a collection of atoms. If I take 4 atoms of Hidrogen I don't have a Helium, I'll have instead 2 molecules of Hidrogen gas.<br /> <br /> In Emergent Patterns it matters quite a lot how the individual constituents of a pattern are arranged, rather than just what those are.<br /> <br /> If I take 6 atoms of Carbon and Oxygen and 12 of Hidrogen I will NOT have a molecule of glucose, unless they are organized in the proper structure that Glucose has.<br /> <br /> There's a phenomenon in chemistry called &quot;Isomery&quot; that is exactly about that - molecules with the same kinds and numbers of atoms but different structures, and thus they behave entirely differently.<br /> <br /> This phenomenon holds true for basically anything imaginable in the Universe. Our conscience is more than just the sum of our neurons, but rather an Emergent Pattern derived from their configuration; human societies and cultures are more than the sum of its individuals, but rather the result of how they interact with each other. Galaxies are more than just the sum of their individual stars, but rather how they interact with each other in their very specific distribution.<br /> <br /> This also means that the entire universe is absolutely interconnected like an infinite cosmic web (like I said, I'm an adherent of Superdeterminism). The tiniest particle influences and is at the same time influenced by the entire Universe (the gravity of the farthest galaxy from us still influence us, and our own gravity also influences the farthest away galaxy).<br /> <br /> Therefore yes, chemical reactions are indeed exchanges of energy, but that's what the study of chemistry entails already. Therefore I think that the Sphere of Matter should deal with that exact kind of energy exchange (as opposed for example from the energy of photons or kinetic or thermal energy which is energy from the movement of molecules). Therefore, I don't think it's necessary to add Energy into it. Moreover, there wouldn't really be anything that Matter would be capable to do by its own if that was the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T22:46:24-07:00","id":1538704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385360-fields-for-the-technocracy-reloaded?p=1538699#post1538699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to agree. <i>If</i> the Matter Field ends up getting the ability to craft Wonders, it should be harder to do that than to use Utility for the task. And I'm thinking that the Matter Field shouldn't have that ability. That's why I said \u201ctake inspiration from\u201d, not \u201ccopy it verbatim\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that, in your configuration, maybe the ability to make Wonders should fall under Void instead<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Agreed. But note that the Utility version of this involves investing points of Primal Energy (or whatever it's called in the context of Utility) into the Venture that you want to bless; the Entropy version doesn't. Wherever the Entropy version ends up, its edge over the Utility version is that it doesn't cost PE to use it. </div> </div> </div>I once created the &quot;Sphere of Memetics&quot;. Just for some context, the idea of &quot;Memetics&quot; was created by Richard Dawkins in his book &quot;Selfish Gene&quot; (great book by the way), upon which at the very end he did a small intellectual exercise, comparing the propagation of ideas to the propagation of genes, insofar that the ideas that &quot;stick&quot; in a society are those that are &quot;stable&quot; (don't change much) and &quot;propagate fast&quot; (just like successful genes), and he named those, the smallest &quot;set of ideas&quot; possible as &quot;meme&quot;, in analogy for the gene but for &quot;the mind&quot;. So a &quot;meme&quot; is like a &quot;mental gene&quot;.<br /> <br /> From this, came the Sci Fi idea of &quot;Science of Memetic&quot;, which I read about once long ago for a scenario that is playable in Gurps and I immediately fell in love. In that futurist scenario, &quot;Memetic&quot; is one of the most dangerous things in the world, and governments have many &quot;Memetic Scientists&quot; constantly on the lookout for &quot;dangerous rogue memes&quot;, because there are memes so virulent, and that's exactly the world, that they can &quot;infect&quot; anyone not &quot;immunized&quot;, and bad actors have become so good in Memetics that they can hide dangerous memes in innocuous and apparently innocent propaganda; for example, an image of a beautiful sunset with what appears to be a positive message may actually be a hidden psychotic message designed by a psychopath master memeticist that causes people to go on a killing spree frenzy (ok, I'm going at the uttermost extreme here of what the setting allows, but it is to better illustrate it).<br /> <br /> I immediately fell in love with this idea and immediately thought &quot;that's as Technocracy as it gets&quot;.<br /> <br /> Now, if I were to do anything in that direction, it would be in this manner. Name it &quot;Memetic Sciences&quot; and call it a day.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T23:32:06-07:00","id":1538706,"title":"","content":"Oh, and if I may, I don't think you need to remove kinetic energy out of Energy, I think it weakens it too much. I know that you think that removing connections and digital web from Space weakens it, but truth is that this is one of the strongest Spheres there are.<br /> <br /> Besides, Space manipulation can also move stuff around, just by different means. &quot;Movement&quot; in the sense of Kinetic energy is also too thematic to be removed from Energy. And, one of the main things of the modern world revolves around turning movement into electricity.<br /> <br /> I also think you should move Utility away from the idea of &quot;alternative Prime&quot; altogether. Whatever &quot;Prime-ish&quot; stuff should go into Void, and let Utility become something entirely new which deals with... Utility lol. Forget &quot;Ventures&quot;. Utility is &quot;Memetic Sciences&quot;, aka mass brainwash propaganda. &quot;Fake News&quot; en masse. It is all that roughly Entropy 5 does, but in a scale, with different degrees. A sort of politics+sociology science. Diplomacy, politics, propaganda, organizational skills. The wet dream of all the managerial class of bureocrats.<br /> <br /> I like Data, very much. So, now the Digital Web is a Realm of pure information rather than some weird ass spacial oddity? I very much like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T23:48:47-07:00","id":1538708,"title":"","content":"So, I think we can wrap up what each Sphere will encompass, don't you think Dataweaver? So now, if you may, please do a little recap with all that you liked so that we may see there's any changes, so that we can take the next step towards defining each lvl","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T01:09:02-07:00","id":1538719,"title":"","content":"I caution against using LLMs for 'hard' information like physics. Their architecture isn't good for accommodating complex relations, hence why ChatGPT is confusing a few different things in the replies: As with many terms, the meaning of 'Information' in physics changes with <a href=\"https://encyclopedia.pub/entry/28489\" target=\"_blank\">context</a>.<br /> <br /> For the purpose of this thread though it serves to justify the integration of Entropy into the Data Sphere via Shannon Entropy, and so far the combination looks successful to me.<br /> <br /> A while ago I tried something similar and rearrange the Spheres based on the SI Units, but fell into a loop of inter-relationships that would render some spheres obsolete. Things like 'Time is a dimension' and 'Matter is Energy equivalent' can trip you up something fierce, so I canned the whole thing. I don't want to discourage exploring alternative Spheres, just caution not to fall into the same trap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T05:48:52-07:00","id":1538730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385360-fields-for-the-technocracy-reloaded?p=1538704#post1538704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that, in your configuration, maybe the ability to make Wonders should fall under Void instead</div> </div> </div> </div>Not Void; Utility. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385360-fields-for-the-technocracy-reloaded?p=1538704#post1538704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I once created the &quot;Sphere of Memetics&quot;. Just for some context, the idea of &quot;Memetics&quot; was created by Richard Dawkins in his book &quot;Selfish Gene&quot; (great book by the way), upon which at the very end he did a small intellectual exercise, comparing the propagation of ideas to the propagation of genes, insofar that the ideas that &quot;stick&quot; in a society are those that are &quot;stable&quot; (don't change much) and &quot;propagate fast&quot; (just like successful genes), and he named those, the smallest &quot;set of ideas&quot; possible as &quot;meme&quot;, in analogy for the gene but for &quot;the mind&quot;. So a &quot;meme&quot; is like a &quot;mental gene&quot;.<br /> <br /> From this, came the Sci Fi idea of &quot;Science of Memetic&quot;, which I read about once long ago for a scenario that is playable in Gurps and I immediately fell in love. In that futurist scenario, &quot;Memetic&quot; is one of the most dangerous things in the world, and governments have many &quot;Memetic Scientists&quot; constantly on the lookout for &quot;dangerous rogue memes&quot;, because there are memes so virulent, and that's exactly the world, that they can &quot;infect&quot; anyone not &quot;immunized&quot;, and bad actors have become so good in Memetics that they can hide dangerous memes in innocuous and apparently innocent propaganda; for example, an image of a beautiful sunset with what appears to be a positive message may actually be a hidden psychotic message designed by a psychopath master memeticist that causes people to go on a killing spree frenzy (ok, I'm going at the uttermost extreme here of what the setting allows, but it is to better illustrate it).<br /> <br /> I immediately fell in love with this idea and immediately thought &quot;that's as Technocracy as it gets&quot;.<br /> <br /> Now, if I were to do anything in that direction, it would be in this manner. Name it &quot;Memetic Sciences&quot; and call it a day.</div> </div> </div> </div>That strikes me as more of a Mind thing. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T06:27:02-07:00","id":1538737,"title":"","content":"If I may: <br /> <br /> In terms of \u201cpedantic and boring groundwork\u201d, Einstein's General Theory of Relativity is a theory of gravity, that expresses it in terms of a curved spacetime geometry. Surprisingly, most of that curvature in practice is in the dimension of time: it turns out that when there's a differential in how fast time flows, trajectories curve toward the region where time is flowing faster. This would argue for the possibility of having Time cover gravity as well. Note that it doesn't take much: Earth's surface gravity is caused by a differential in the flow of time so small that it takes careful examination of highly precise atomic clocks to measure it, making it a significant factor in our GPS network which involves placing highly precise atomic clocks in orbit, where the flow of time hasn't been altered by gravity nearly as much as it has been on the planet's surface. <br /> <br /> Space would also have some limited influence here, as large differentials in motion tend to generate a \u201cframe dragging effect\u201d that similarly alters trajectories to equalize the disparate motions. This is most notably seen in the case of a rapidly spinning black hole (as in, rotation near the speed of light), where trajectories approaching its surface find themselves forced to circle around the black hole; and in some cases, this space curvature is so severe that the \u201cdirection of time\u201d tilts <i>sideways </i>into what would normally be a direction of space, and the timeline of whatever follows that trajectory ends up doing an \u201coroboros\u201d, circling around the spinning black hole until the path's future encounters its past and the snake eats its tail. <br /> <br /> The point is that the Enlightened Science notion of Time and Space isn't the classic view of everything matching forward through Time at a single, steady pace, with Space being a featureless background. Motion is the interplay between Space and Time, and gravity is what happens when that interplay gets distorted. This is why I think that motion should be governed by Space, and gravity should perhaps be governed by Time. <br /> <br /> Where energy and momentum come in is that they're what traditionally <i>cause </i>the spacetime distortions. I agree now that motion and gravity shouldn't be removed from the domain of Energy; but they should also be covered by Space and perhaps Time as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T06:38:00-07:00","id":1538739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385360-fields-for-the-technocracy-reloaded?p=1538719#post1538719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I caution against using LLMs for 'hard' information like physics. Their architecture isn't good for accommodating complex relations, hence why ChatGPT is confusing a few different things in the replies: As with many terms, the meaning of 'Information' in physics changes with <a href=\"https://encyclopedia.pub/entry/28489\" target=\"_blank\">context</a>.<br /> <br /> For the purpose of this thread though it serves to justify the integration of Entropy into the Data Sphere via Shannon Entropy, and so far the combination looks successful to me.<br /> <br /> A while ago I tried something similar and rearrange the Spheres based on the SI Units, but fell into a loop of inter-relationships that would render some spheres obsolete. Things like 'Time is a dimension' and 'Matter is Energy equivalent' can trip you up something fierce, so I canned the whole thing. I don't want to discourage exploring alternative Spheres, just caution not to fall into the same trap.</div> </div> </div> </div>This reminds me of a comic strip I saw once: <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><figure class=\"image bbcode-attachment align_center\"><a href=\"https://xkcd.com/435\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img alt=\"Purity of the Scientific Fields\" title=\"xkcd purity test\" width=\"740\" height=\"308\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://xkcd.com/435\" data-linktarget=\"1\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://imgs.xkcd.com/comics/purity.png\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://imgs.xkcd.com/comics/purity.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://imgs.xkcd.com/comics/purity.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"Fields of Science\" class=\"bbcode-attachment js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/></a><figcaption>Fields of Science</figcaption></figure></div> <br /> <br /> As things stand, it looks like Primal Utility covers economists (not pictured) and sociologists; Mind covers psychologists; Life covers biologists; Matter covers chemists; Energy covers physicists; and Data covers mathematicians.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":".  Fixed Caption 07-17-2024, 09:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T07:43:39-07:00","id":1538748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385360-fields-for-the-technocracy-reloaded?p=1538719#post1538719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I caution against using LLMs for 'hard' information like physics. Their architecture isn't good for accommodating complex relations, hence why ChatGPT is confusing a few different things in the replies: As with many terms, the meaning of 'Information' in physics changes with <a href=\"https://encyclopedia.pub/entry/28489\" target=\"_blank\">context</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes I know. It was just to guide the thoughts in a more concise manner (I'm too prolix, I just can't for the love of me be concise, so I opted to let a more organized &quot;mind&quot; help me out)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For the purpose of this thread though it serves to justify the integration of Entropy into the Data Sphere via Shannon Entropy, and so far the combination looks successful to me. </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A while ago I tried something similar and rearrange the Spheres based on the SI Units, but fell into a loop of inter-relationships that would render some spheres obsolete. Things like 'Time is a dimension' and 'Matter is Energy equivalent' can trip you up something fierce, so I canned the whole thing. I don't want to discourage exploring alternative Spheres, just caution not to fall into the same trap. </div> </div> </div>Yes, I agree. Which is why I also recommend keeping Energy and Matter as separate as possible, just like Physics and Chemistry. In my games however, I use Biochemistry and Time/Space Spheres for Techies, but I also use several other hacks for several other groups in fully customized Spheres.<br /> <br /> I did like the ideas of Dataweaver about Utility and Void, so perhaps I may get something from that for my own and perhaps ditch Prime entirely <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":